### Summary
After the Control UI lists Claude sessions once, the macOS app's node worker (`openclaw-node-worker`, running under Bun) rescans `~/.claude/projects` and the Claude Desktop session store every second for as long as it runs, even when nothing reads the catalog.

### Steps to reproduce
From source (fresh state, no Gateway, no credentials):

1. Check out `main` (reproduced at `ec702e83388`), run `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`, and use Bun 1.4.4.
2. Create a synthetic projects tree: `R=$(mktemp -d)`, then 40 directories under `$R/projects`, each with 24 one-line `.jsonl` transcripts (script in Logs below).
3. Run the harness in Logs below under Bun: `bun idle.ts "$PWD" "$R/projects" 65 30`. In a source checkout without a built plugin SDK, `openclaw/plugin-sdk/*` has to resolve to `src/plugin-sdk/*.ts` (for example a local `node_modules/openclaw/package.json` that maps those exports). It calls `readProjectsTreeSnapshot` once (the function behind `anthropic.claude.sessions.list.v1`), waits 65 s with no further reads, then measures process CPU for 30 s.
4. Optional: subscribe to the same tree with fs-safe `watch({ mode: "auto" })` under Bun and print `health()`. It reports `{"state":"ready","mode":"poll","directories":41}`.

On the macOS app:

1. Run OpenClaw.app as a node connected to a Gateway, on a Mac where `~/.claude/projects` has sessions.
2. Open the dashboard and let the sidebar show Claude sessions once.
3. Close the dashboard window. Do not use OpenClaw for 2 minutes.
4. Find the worker (the child of `OpenClaw.app/Contents/MacOS/OpenClaw` whose process title is `openclaw-node-worker`) and run `sample <pid> 8`. Measure CPU with `ps -o time= -p <pid>` at the start and end of 60 s windows.

### Expected behavior
With no catalog reader, the worker does no recurring per-second filesystem work for the Claude catalog. Reference: the Control UI deliberately stops listing while the page is hidden (`ui/src/components/session-data-catalog.ts:166`), and OpenClaw's own polling fallback for config sources reconciles every 5 minutes "without frequent idle wakeups" (`src/infra/fs-observation-mode.ts:1-2`).

### Actual behavior
Under Bun, fs-safe 0.27.1 `watch({ mode: "auto" })` has no qualified event transport, so it falls back to a guarded poll that rescans the tree every 1000 ms on the main thread. The catalog arms two of these watches on its first list and never closes them:

- `~/.claude/projects`, depth 2 (`extensions/anthropic/session-catalog-scan.ts:284`)
- `~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude-code-sessions`, depth 3 (`extensions/anthropic/session-catalog-desktop.ts:567`)

Both go through `createDirtyDirectoryWatch` (`extensions/anthropic/session-catalog-tree-watch.ts:30`). The Control UI stops listing while hidden, so every tick after that runs with no reader.

Source repro, Bun 1.4.4 on macOS (Apple silicon), 960 synthetic transcripts, 65 s after the last read, one 30 s window per case:

| Case | Idle CPU (% of one core) | RSS |
|---|---|---|
| Same harness and imports, no catalog read (control) | 0.04% | 39-40 MB |
| One catalog read | 1.51% | 50-52 MB |

### OpenClaw version
2026.10.10 (installed macOS app). Also reproduced from source on `main` at `ec702e83388`.

### Operating system
macOS 27.2 (arm64)

### Install method
mac app (node mode); source checkout for the harness repro

### Model
Not applicable: no model request is involved. The worker is idle.

### Provider / routing chain
Not applicable: no model request is involved.

### Additional provider/model setup details
Not applicable.

### Logs
