## What Problem This Solves

Voice Call cannot currently keep agent consultation available while making the delegated run's tool surface fail closed.

## User Impact

Operators can select a tool-free consultation mode for informational or policy-bounded realtime voice workflows. Existing `safe-read-only`, `owner`, and `none` behavior and defaults are unchanged.

## Why This Change Was Made

This adds explicit `realtime.toolPolicy: "consult-no-tools"` across the shared policy type and Voice Call manifest. In this mode:

- the provider can call `openclaw_agent_consult`;
- configured/custom realtime function tools are omitted;
- the existing `openclaw_end_call` lifecycle control remains available on function-tool providers; native-delegation providers reject this mode because hang-up requires their call-scoped delegated tool;
- the embedded agent receives `toolsAllow: []` and `disableTools: true`;
- routed agent workspace, sandbox session identity, and stricter authority overlays remain intact.

This is enforced during capability construction rather than relying on prompt instructions or a dummy tool.

